# Project 3 — Linux Account & Access Management

## Project Overview

This project focused on Linux account management, user provisioning, group-based access control, password management, privilege separation, and account verification on a Raspberry Pi running Raspberry Pi OS.

The goal was to simulate a small organization's user-management environment by creating different user roles, assigning users to appropriate security groups, configuring passwords, controlling administrative privileges, and verifying that users only had the access intended for their role.

This project was performed remotely through SSH from a 2015 MacBook Air to the Raspberry Pi.

