# Phase 1 — Establish Remote Administration

The project was performed remotely from the 2015 MacBook Air using SSH.

The MacBook Air connected to the Raspberry Pi using:

ssh dedfr@10.0.0.98

After authentication, the remote shell displayed:

dedfr@raspberrypi:~ $

This confirmed that the MacBook Air could remotely administer the Raspberry Pi.

The remote session was verified using:

whoami

hostname

uptime

These commands confirmed:

- The authenticated account was dedfr.
- The remote system was the Raspberry Pi.
- The SSH connection was providing an interactive remote Linux shell.

