# Security Concepts Demonstrated

This project demonstrated several important cybersecurity and Linux administration concepts.

## 1. Principle of Least Privilege

Users should only receive the permissions required for their job.

The developer account was intentionally prevented from using sudo.

## 2. Role-Based Access Control

Groups were used to organize users according to their responsibilities.

Examples:

cybersecurity

developers

labadmins

## 3. Privilege Separation

Administrative access was separated from normal user access.

The analyst account received sudo privileges while the developer account did not.

## 4. Authentication Management

Individual passwords were created and managed for separate user accounts.

## 5. Password Lifecycle Management

Password aging and status information were examined using Linux account-management utilities.

## 6. Account Verification

User IDs, groups, passwords, and sudo privileges were verified after configuration.

## 7. Remote Administration

All administration was performed remotely using SSH from the 2015 MacBook Air.

